<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- The web engine's host and the helpers that run no code of the web (plan 99): nothing
     beyond the hardened runtime. The renderer and the GPU helper have files of their own
     (web-engine-renderer.entitlements, web-engine-gpu.entitlements).

     The workflow adds com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation to every
     executable's entitlements: without an Apple Team ID (ad hoc or the project's
     self-signed certificate), the hardened runtime refuses to load the framework into
     the host and its helpers. With a real Team ID, the entitlement is harmless. The app
     also re-signs after downloading when the entitlement is missing (install/mod.rs). -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
